Result files in the formats bmb_report must refuse (#1, decision 5), laid
out exactly as those versions wrote them -- recovered from the git history
(git show v0.5.0:src/c/common/bmb_print.c), not reconstructed from memory.

  v0.5.0.json    before 0.6.0: no version, no backend, time_s was a mean
  v0.6.1.json    0.6.x: no machine information, no dimension labels
  v2.0.0.json    a future major version
  not-ours.json  JSON from something else entirely

Current-format input is not kept here: the tests generate it by running the
benchmarks, so it can never fall out of date.
